+# Architecture v2
 
-## Data layer
+## Pipeline
 
-1. `MarketDataClient` downloads closed 1-hour BTC perpetual candles.
-2. A complete 180-day dataset is selected from one provider only.
-3. SQLite stores candles, news, signals and runtime events.
-4. Duplicate timestamps, missing rows and excessive gaps are rejected.
+`Market data -> Leakage-safe hourly features -> Regime engine -> Independent event detector -> Direction/tradeability models -> Per-horizon qualification -> Fail-safe decision -> Paper resolution`
 
-## Feature layer
+## Regime engine
 
-The feature vector is available only after a candle has closed. It contains:
+- KAMA efficiency-adaptive trend
+- ADX and DI spread
+- ATR and volatility percentile
+- Donchian location and channel width
+- Bollinger width percentile
 
-- EMA20 and EMA50 spread, slopes and price distance
-- bullish/bearish cross events
-- hours since the latest cross
-- return since cross
-- returns and realized volatility from 1 to 48 hours
-- ATR14, RSI14, body and wick geometry
-- volume and trade-count surprises
-- hourly and weekday cyclic encodings
-- news volume, relevance and sentiment over 1/3/6/12/24 hours
+## Events
 
-The first three hours after a cross receive the highest training weight. The remaining hours inside the 12-hour event window receive a lower but still elevated weight.
+Events are emitted only on the confirming closed candle and receive a unique ID. Same-direction events are deduplicated for the configured cooldown.
 
-## Model layer
+- `DONCHIAN_BREAKOUT`
+- `SQUEEZE_RELEASE`
+- `PULLBACK_RESUME`
+- `VOLUME_IMPULSE`
 
-For each horizon (1h, 2h, 3h):
+## Targets
 
-- HistGradientBoostingClassifier estimates `P(UP)`.
-- Logistic Regression supplies a lower-variance linear baseline.
-- Their probabilities are blended.
-- HistGradientBoostingRegressor estimates future return.
+At event candle `t`, the reference entry is `open[t+1]`. For horizon `h`, the target close is `close[t+h]`. Labels include raw direction, tradeability after cost buffer, MFE, MAE and conservative triple-barrier outcome.
 
-The aggregate forecast always becomes `UP` or `DOWN`. There is no neutral class.
+## Models
 
-## Decision layer
+Each horizon contains:
 
-A forecast is converted into a paper-trade plan only when:
+- blended gradient-boosting and logistic direction classifier;
+- absolute-error return regressor;
+- event-only tradeability classifier;
+- temporal Platt-style probability calibrator when enough calibration data exists.
 
-- model qualification passed;
-- current candle is inside the post-cross window;
-- 1h/2h/3h forecasts sufficiently agree;
-- confidence is adequate;
-- expected gross movement exceeds stressed costs plus required edge;
-- ATR is valid and no volatility shock exists;
-- candle source, model source and live quote source remain consistent;
-- signal limits and cooldown pass.
+## Decision separation
 
-Otherwise the forecast remains visible while action becomes `WAIT`.
+The forecast is always binary UP/DOWN. The action can be WAIT when a new event is absent, the horizon is unqualified, costs consume the expected edge, data is stale or a risk limit is active.
