-# Fail-safe design
+# Fail-safe v2
 
-The system defaults to not trading.
+A paper action is blocked when any applicable condition is present:
 
-## Data safety
+- incompatible v1 model artifact;
+- no newly confirmed market event;
+- Event ID already traded;
+- selected horizon not qualified;
+- low direction confidence;
+- low tradeability probability;
+- horizon disagreement;
+- expected edge below stress execution cost and profit buffer;
+- stale quote, provider mismatch or candle gap;
+- excessive ATR volatility;
+- configured news shock;
+- daily signal limit or cooldown;
+- stale model.
 
-- closed candles only;
-- duplicate removal;
-- maximum allowed gap check;
-- minimum 180-day row coverage;
-- source lock between training and live inference;
-- stale quote detection;
-- missing-news indicator rather than fabricated sentiment.
-
-## Model safety
-
-- temporal walk-forward validation;
-- model-age check and optional weekly retraining;
-- model qualification blocks actions but not visibility;
-- separate UP/DOWN forecast and LONG/SHORT/WAIT action;
-- horizon-agreement requirement.
-
-## Financial safety
-
-- paper-only mode;
-- no exchange credentials or order endpoint;
-- transaction-cost stress multiplier;
-- ATR-based stop;
-- minimum and maximum stop distance;
-- fixed fractional risk sizing;
-- leverage capped at 3x;
-- daily signal cap and cooldown.
-
-## Runtime safety
-
-- every new live/dashboard process resets the eligibility clock;
-- first suggestion is allowed only after the next complete one-hour candle;
-- exceptions are stored as `FAIL_SAFE` runtime events;
-- no stale signal is silently reused.
+UP/DOWN remains visible even when action is WAIT. Live order execution is not implemented.
